-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Checked after rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52914, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RzLVvz5mfNfkBAh3HM7wSu", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52914, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RzLVvz5mfNfkBAh3HM7wSu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 56806, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. I rolled it back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before. Since the rollback, the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 says what failed, what I did and the status after the rollback. It also notes that the v2.3.1 test build (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging, so the problem was visible before the production deploy.\n- **Next step:** v2.3.1 shouldn't be redeployed until someone finds the cause.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JCn3wT7M6SgGtRy7ASuQx6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014uZ8gogzjvB5N59AzUGuvi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PWRTjthENEriS1XFnk8VZM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VYewzVA8nDmcfnTHYBfEH3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019ASwThCoZ7NvK7wnqqxVVu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RzLVvz5mfNfkBAh3HM7wSu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Checked after rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. I rolled it back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before. Since the rollback, the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 says what failed, what I did and the status after the rollback. It also notes that the v2.3.1 test build (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging, so the problem was visible before the production deploy.\n- **Next step:** v2.3.1 shouldn't be redeployed until someone finds the cause.", "type": "text"}]}]}